<p>North Korean leader Kim Jong Un and Belarusian President Alexander Lukashenko signed a friendship and cooperation treaty in Pyongyang during Lukashenko’s first visit to North Korea. Both governments cast the agreement as a way for independently aligned states to work more closely under international pressure. The visit included a formal welcome ceremony, military pageantry and bilateral talks, making the growing ties between two governments under Western sanctions and closely aligned with Russia hard to miss. The meeting carries weight beyond symbolism. The sources describe both countries as key supporters of Russia’s war in Ukraine, and their closer coordination comes amid broader tensions with the United States and its allies. State media in both countries framed the treaty around sovereignty, political stability and economic development, while outside reporting pointed to the wider geopolitical backdrop, including estimates that around 2,000 North Korean soldiers are thought to have died supporting Russia’s war effort.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DMqGH6zCTaLDyBnGbKGaaL5-U-Ltn5VTCC0gAFjH20KZ_mccPlIUTX_-gc-rHYky4obtmcJayilzQ8BVWgxWRdNYa4HGTXWiIuk3XUGfGetA' alt='Belarusian President Alexander Lukashenko and North Korea’s Kim Jong Un attend a signing ceremony in Pyongyang, North Korea, in an image released on March 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceremonial display: North Korean media showed Kim welcoming Lukashenko with an artillery salute, goose-stepping soldiers and a flag-waving crowd at the start of the two-day visit.</li><li>Symbolic gift: The BBC said Lukashenko gave Kim a rifle during the visit, adding a striking personal gesture to the treaty signing.</li><li>Banquet follow-up: Dawn’s report included KCNA-released images of Kim and Lukashenko attending a banquet in Pyongyang after the signing, extending the visit’s carefully staged hospitality.</li><li>Memorial stop: Lukashenko also visited the Kumsusan Palace of the Sun, where Kim’s father and grandfather lie in state, underscoring the ceremonial importance North Korea attached to the trip.</li></ul><blockquote>In the modern realities of global transformation — at a time when the world’s major powers openly ignore and violate the norms of international law — independent countries must cooperate more closely and consolidate their efforts aimed at protecting their sovereignty and improving the well-being of their citizens - Alexander Lukashenko</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>BBC framing: The BBC highlighted Lukashenko’s gift of a rifle to Kim as the visit’s most striking personal symbol, portraying the summit as both a show of leader-to-leader affinity and official diplomacy between two supporters of Russia’s war in Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8957dxjvkxo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Kim Jong Un: North Korea’s leader voiced support for Belarus against what he called illegitimate Western pressure and backed Belarusian steps aimed at social and political stability and economic development. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985838/north-korea-belarus-sign-friendship-treaty-during-lukashenko-visit'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>ABC News analysis: ABC described the two governments as key allies of Moscow drawing closer while confronting the United States and its partners, placing the treaty in a wider strategic alignment rather than a purely bilateral relationship. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korea-belarus-leaders-meet-pyongyang-sign-friendship-131423611'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985838/north-korea-belarus-sign-friendship-treaty-during-lukashenko-visit'>North Korea, Belarus sign ‘friendship’ treaty during Lukashenko visit</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/diplomacy/article/3348067/north-korea-and-belarus-sign-friendship-treaty-lukashenkos-first-visit'>North Korea and Belarus sign friendship treaty on Lukashenko’s first visit</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korea-belarus-leaders-meet-pyongyang-sign-friendship-131423611'>North Korea, Belarus leaders meet in Pyongyang, sign friendship treaty</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8957dxjvkxo'>Belarus leader gifts rifle to North Korea&#x27;s Kim as they sign friendship treaty</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/26/north-korea-belarus-friendship-cooperation-treaty'>Belarus and North Korea sign a &quot;friendship and cooperation&quot; treaty after North Korean supreme leader Kim Jong Un welcomed Belarusian president Alexander Lukashenko to Pyongyang.</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>